= Vote of Confidence for Chancellor Scholz

Scholz has called a Vote of Confidence after the collapse of the <span style="color: [+ spd_color +];">Traffic</span> <span style="color: [+ greens_color +];">Light</span> <span style="color: [+ fdp_color +];">coalition</span>. There seems to be no possible coalition to form, so Scholz's hope is to trigger a snap election as soon as possible.

As for us, we haven't been approached by any of the member parties. We probably shouldn't concern ourselves with what doesn't regard us. Still, shall we vote for or against Scholz?

- @for: Vote in favor of the Chancellor, thereby potentially saving the government.
- @against: Vote against the Chancellor, as expected.

@for
go-to: against if ((spd_b + greens_b + linke_b) < 50); election_1928.ministries if (spd_b + greens_b + linke_b)>= 50

@against
on-arrival: ampelkoalition = 0; next_election_year = year if month <= 9; next_election_year = (year+1) if month > 9; next_election_month = (month+3) if (month+3) <= 12; next_election_month = (month-9) if (month+3) > 12; pro_status_quo -= 3;

Scholz has lost the vote, as expected. Next elections will be set for [+ next_election_month +] [+ next_election_year +].
